{
  "title": "Report failed games as failed or partial orchestrator runs",
  "description": "run_orchestrator returns exit_code=0 after runtime game \
failures. In batch mode, setup failures are logged and skipped as long as at \
least one session launches. Nonzero spectator results and pilot failures are \
passed to finalize_game, but they do not affect the final exit code. \
post_game_failures are also printed without changing success status. This \
allows callers and automation to treat an incomplete run as successful. Track \
requested, launched, completed, and failed games explicitly; return a nonzero \
result for failed requested work or introduce an unambiguous partial-success \
status that CLI callers translate to failure. Preserve per-session failure \
reasons so tournament and batch callers do not have to infer failure from \
missing winners. Add tests for launch failure, pilot failure, spectator \
failure, and post-game export failure.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 1,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "orchestration",
    "reliability",
  ],
